$ krowk sessions import --help
stdout:
krowk sessions import — Import this machine's agent transcripts

Usage
  krowk sessions import --from <provider|all> [--dry-run] [--limit N]

Flags
  --from <string>            Which transcripts to read: claude, cursor,
                             opencode, ledger (provider usage ledgers), or all.
                             Required
  --dry-run                  Count what would be imported and write nothing
  --limit <int> (default 0)  Read at most this many transcripts per source (0 is
                             all)

Global flags: --workspace --dev --format --json --quiet --jq — see `help flags`
exit: 0

$ krowk uploads --help
stdout:
krowk uploads — List, show, attach or delete uploads

Commands (krowk uploads …)
  create <file...> [flags]  Upload files: the long form of `krowk push`
  list [flags]              List uploads, newest first: a run's, or the
                            workspace's
  show <artifact>           Read one artifact back
  attach <art> --run <run>  Put an upload under a run afterwards
  delete <art> [token]      Take an upload down — immediate, cannot be undone

Global flags: --workspace --dev --format --json --quiet --jq — see `help flags`
exit: 0

